  "details": "In C#, disabling a script or a gameObject will cause all subsequent events in the script to stop firing, even the ones that would run on the same frame. In Udon however, this is not the case.\n\nI've set up a script that disabled the script in Update, then does a debug log during the same frame in LateUpdate. In C#, this late update log does not fire, while in U# LateUpdate logs the same frame as Update did.\n\nThe logging was seen inside of VRChat's client as well, so the issue exists on the UdonVM's side and is not exclusively a U# issue.\n\nIn this example I disable the gameobject, but the exact same behaviour is seen when disabling the script itself.\n\nprivate int count;\n\nprivate void Update()\n\n{\n\n    count++;\n\n    if (count == 100)\n\n    {\n\n        Debug.Log($\"Called disable at {Time.frameCount}\");\n\n        gameObject.SetActive(false);\n\n    }\n\n}\n\nprivate void LateUpdate()\n\n{\n\n    if (count == 100) Debug.Log($\"Count 100 in Late Update {Time.frameCount}\");\n\n}",
